# Paragraphs and line breaks

@lede
Lines that don't begin with a block sigil are paragraph text. Blank lines
separate paragraphs. A trailing backslash forces a line break.
@end

## What counts as a paragraph

A paragraph is one or more consecutive non-blank lines that do not begin
with a block sigil — a `#` heading, a `-` list item, a `>` blockquote, a
`|` table row, an `@` shortcode, a digit-then-`.`-then-space ordered
list, a triple-backtick code fence, a `//` line comment, a `/*` block
comment, or a `---` horizontal rule.

```brief
This is one paragraph
that spans two source lines.

This is the next paragraph.
```

Lines inside a paragraph are joined with a single space when rendered.
Source-level wrapping has no effect on output.

## Hard line breaks

A backslash at the very end of a line is the hard-break marker:

```brief
First line.\
Second line in the same paragraph.
```

Renders as a paragraph with a `<br>` between the two lines (HTML target),
or with a literal newline in LLM mode.

@callout(kind: note)
There is no `@br` shortcode. The trailing backslash is the only canonical
hard-break form — adding a second spelling would break the "one way to
do it" rule.
@end

## Blank lines

Multiple blank lines collapse to a single paragraph break. There is no
"force two paragraph breaks" syntax — a paragraph is a paragraph.

## Paragraphs and other blocks

Paragraphs are interrupted by any block sigil. The compiler does not
require a blank line between a paragraph and the next block, but the
formatter inserts one.

```brief
A paragraph.
- list item
- another list item
A paragraph again.
```

That parses as paragraph → list → paragraph. The list ends as soon as a
non-list line follows.

## Inline content

Inside a paragraph, all inline constructs are valid:

- Emphasis: `*bold*`, `_italic_`, `+underline+`, `~strike~`.
- Inline code: `` `printf` ``.
- Inline shortcodes: `@kbd[Ctrl+C]`, `@math[E = m c^2]`, `@link[text](url)`.
- Escapes: `\*not bold\*`.

See @ref[language/emphasis.brf](Emphasis) and
@ref[language/shortcodes.brf](Shortcodes) for the inline catalog.
